3
00:00:05.586 --> 00:00:08.046
That is called matrilineal.

4
00:00:08.046 --> 00:00:09.946
Descent is traced through the

5
00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:11.266
mother's side.

6
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.666
In India, the Khasi of Meghalaya

7
00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:17.206
and the Nairs of old Kerala are

8
00:00:17.206 --> 00:00:18.656
well known examples.

9
00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.052
The Khasi are the largest

10
00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:23.532
community in Meghalaya, about

11
00:00:23.532 --> 00:00:24.892
forty eight percent of its

12
00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:27.172
people. They are among the few

13
00:00:27.172 --> 00:00:28.872
tribes that still have a

14
00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:30.402
matrilineal society.

15
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:33.507
In a Khasi family, the youngest

16
00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:36.067
